---
// src/pages/about.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="About Chemistrycal | Research-Grade Benchtop Computational Suite"
  description="Learn about Chemistrycal, an open scientific utility suite developed by physical and analytical chemists to eliminate benchtop volumetric errors and provide standardized stoichiometric workflows."
>
  <main style="max-width: 900px; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #1e293b; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;">
    
    <!-- Hero / Mission -->
    <div style="border-bottom: 2px solid #e2e8f0; padding-bottom: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <span style="display: inline-block; background: #e0f2fe; color: #0284c7; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; padding: 0.3rem 0.85rem; border-radius: 9999px; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        Scientific Precision &amp; Transparency
      </span>
      <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; letter-spacing: -0.025em; margin: 0 0 1rem 0;">
        About Chemistrycal
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: #475569; margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
        A research-grade computational suite developed to bridge the gap between theoretical stoichiometry and practical wet-lab formulation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Editorial & Scientific Authority -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Editorial Leadership &amp; Scientific Background
      </h2>
      <p>
        Chemistrycal was founded and is actively maintained by <strong>Bilal Khan</strong>, a physical chemistry researcher and educator based in Hazro, District Attock, Pakistan. His research background encompasses <strong>materials chemistry, metal-organic frameworks (HKUST-1 composites), advanced oxidation processes (AOPs), and solution plasma catalytic degradation</strong>.
      </p>
      
      <!-- Verified Researcher Identity Card / Knowledge Graph Anchors -->
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; margin: 1.25rem 0 1.75rem 0;">
        <a 
          href="https://orcid.org/0009-0006-3082-7043" 
          target="_blank" 
          rel="noopener noreferrer" 
          style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.45rem; background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; padding: 0.4rem 0.85rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 700; color: #334155; transition: all 0.2s ease;"
        >
          <img src="https://orcid.org/assets/vectors/orcid.logo.icon.svg" alt="ORCID Logo" style="width: 16px; height: 16px;" />
          ORCID: 0009-0006-3082-7043
        </a>
        <a 
          href="https://github.com/Hadee017" 
          target="_blank" 
          rel="noopener noreferrer" 
          style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.45rem; background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; padding: 0.4rem 0.85rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 700; color: #334155; transition: all 0.2s ease;"
        >
          <span>💻</span>
          GitHub: @Hadee017
        </a>
        <a 
          href="https://zenodo.org/records/23059466" 
          target="_blank" 
          rel="noopener noreferrer" 
          style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.45rem; background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; padding: 0.4rem 0.85rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 700; color: #334155; transition: all 0.2s ease;"
        >
          <span>📦</span>
          CERN Zenodo Archive
        </a>
      </div>

      <p>
        Having worked extensively across academic synthesis laboratories and practical teaching academies, the founder designed Chemistrycal to solve a persistent lab failure point: the discrepancy between theoretical textbook formulas and practical balance weighing—specifically accounting for <em>crystalline hydration water (&middot;nH₂O)</em>, manufacturer <em>assay purity percentages</em>, and <em>instrumental X-ray peak broadening</em>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Standards & Methodological Accuracy -->
    <section style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 12px; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Computational &amp; Analytical Standards
      </h2>
      <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        All calculators on Chemistrycal adhere strictly to internationally recognized scientific conventions:
      </p>
      <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #334155;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">
          <strong>IUPAC Standard Atomic Weights:</strong> Formula masses are computed from standard isotope abundances to four decimal places.
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">
          <strong>Hydration Stoichiometry:</strong> Hydrate molecular contributions explicitly track molar water mass (18.01528 g/mol) to prevent systematic molarity deficits.
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">
          <strong>Scherrer Crystallite Deconvolution:</strong> PXRD peak broadening evaluations incorporate full instrumental baseline subtraction (b<sub>std</sub>) and shape factors (K = 0.94).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Client-Side Execution:</strong> All numerical evaluations execute directly within the user's browser using double-precision arithmetic. Proprietary experimental parameters and research formulations are never transmitted to external servers.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Academic Citation & Archival -->
    <section style="background: #ffffff; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 12px; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin: 0;">
          Academic Archival &amp; Citation
        </h2>
        <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23059466" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <img 
            src="https://zenodo.org/badge/DOI/10.5281/zenodo.23059466.svg" 
            alt="Zenodo DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.23059466"
            style="height: 26px; vertical-align: middle;" 
          />
        </a>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        Chemistrycal is registered and permanently archived in CERN's open-access repository via Zenodo. If you employ this computational suite in thesis dissertations, peer-reviewed manuscripts, or standard laboratory protocol documentation, please cite the permanent record:
      </p>
      <pre style="background: #0f172a; color: #e2e8f0; padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.6; overflow-x: auto; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace; margin: 0;">
@software&#123;chemistrycal_2026,
  author       = &#123;Khan, Bilal&#125;,
  title        = &#123;Chemistrycal: A Client-Side Computational Suite for Analytical Stoichiometry, Solution Formulations, and Powder Diffraction Crystallite Domain Analysis&#125;,
  publisher    = &#123;Zenodo&#125;,
  year         = &#123;2026&#125;,
  doi          = &#123;10.5281/zenodo.23059466&#125;,
  url          = &#123;https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23059466&#125;
&#125;</pre>
    </section>

    <!-- Open Access & Contact Info -->
    <section>
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Peer Review &amp; Method Verification
      </h2>
      <p>
        Chemistrycal is an open educational and laboratory utility. If you identify a formula edge case, require a specific reagent addition to our database, or wish to propose an analytical workflow collaboration, please reach out directly through our <a href="/contact" style="color: #0284c7; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none;">Contact Page</a>.
      </p>
      <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #64748b; margin-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; padding-top: 1rem;">
        <em>Last Methodological Review: October 2026 | Compliant with standard analytical laboratory operating procedures.</em>
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>